{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Gradient Descent Lab\n",
    "\n",
    "Explore the mechanics of gradient descent: tracking cost curves and line fitting side-by-side, verifying the 1/2 convention, investigating cost convexity, exploring the runaway behavior of gradient ascent, observing automatic step-shrinking (braking), and measuring how feature scaling directly affects convergence iterations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Helper Functions\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's define standard cost and gradient helper functions, as well as a non-convex MSE-on-sigmoid cost function."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def cost(X, y, th, half=False):\n",
    "    return np.sum((X @ th - y) ** 2) / ((2 if half else 1) * len(y))\n",
    "\n",
    "def grad(X, y, th, half=False):\n",
    "    return ((1 if half else 2) / len(y)) * X.T @ (X @ th - y)\n",
    "\n",
    "def sig_cost(X, y, th):\n",
    "    return np.sum((1 / (1 + np.exp(-np.clip(X @ th, -500, 500))) - y) ** 2) / len(y)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Two Curves, One Run\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's track cost and predictions concurrently. Notice how cost converges long before individual coefficients."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "n, alpha = 50, 0.1\n",
    "xf = np.random.randn(n, 1)\n",
    "xf = (xf - xf.mean()) / xf.std()\n",
    "y = 2 * xf.ravel() + 5 + np.random.randn(n) * 0.5\n",
    "X = np.c_[np.ones(n), xf]\n",
    "th_ols = np.linalg.lstsq(X, y, rcond=None)[0]\n",
    "eig = np.linalg.eigvalsh((2 / n) * (X.T @ X))\n",
    "x_at = np.array([-2.0, 0.0, 2.0])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"1. TWO CURVES FROM ONE RUN   (cost vs iteration, and the line in data space)\")\n",
    "print(f\"   n = {n}, feature standardised -> kappa = {eig.max() / eig.min():.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   {'iter':>5}{'b':>10}{'w':>10}{'J':>11}{'\u2016\u2207J\u2016':>10}{'\u1e71(\u22122)':>10}{'\u1e71(0)':>10}{'\u1e71(+2)':>10}\")\n",
    "th = np.zeros(2)\n",
    "for i in range(101):\n",
    "    if i in (0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100):\n",
    "        a = th[0] + th[1] * x_at\n",
    "        print(f\"   {i:>5}{th[0]:>10.5f}{th[1]:>10.5f}{cost(X, y, th):>11.5f}\"\n",
    "              f\"{np.linalg.norm(grad(X, y, th)):>10.5f}{a[0]:>10.5f}{a[1]:>10.5f}{a[2]:>10.5f}\")\n",
    "    if i < 100:\n",
    "        th = th - alpha * grad(X, y, th)\n",
    "a = th_ols[0] + th_ols[1] * x_at\n",
    "print(f\"   {'OLS':>5}{th_ols[0]:>10.5f}{th_ols[1]:>10.5f}{cost(X, y, th_ols):>11.5f}\"\n",
    "      f\"{0.0:>10.5f}{a[0]:>10.5f}{a[1]:>10.5f}{a[2]:>10.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. The 1/2 Convention\n",
    "\n",
    "Observe how halving the cost halves the gradient, which acts exactly like halving the learning rate."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"2. THE 1/2 CONVENTION   (same problem, three runs)\")\n",
    "print(f\"   {'iter':>5}{'J=(1/n) a=0.1':>16}{'J=(1/2n) a=0.1':>17}\"\n",
    "      f\"{'J=(1/2n) a=0.2':>17}{'col1/col3':>11}\")\n",
    "ta, tb, tc = np.zeros(2), np.zeros(2), np.zeros(2)\n",
    "for i in range(5):\n",
    "    ca, cb, cc = cost(X, y, ta), cost(X, y, tb, True), cost(X, y, tc, True)\n",
    "    print(f\"   {i:>5}{ca:>16.8f}{cb:>17.8f}{cc:>17.8f}{ca / cc:>11.8f}\")\n",
    "    ta = ta - 0.1 * grad(X, y, ta)\n",
    "    tb = tb - 0.1 * grad(X, y, tb, True)\n",
    "    tc = tc - 0.2 * grad(X, y, tc, True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Convexity, Measured\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's run 2,000 random chord midpoint checks to find violations of convexity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"3. CONVEXITY   (midpoint chord test, 2000 random parameter pairs)\")\n",
    "for name, fn, box in ((\"MSE\", cost, 10.0), (\"MSE of sigmoid(X\u03b8)\", sig_cost, 5.0)):\n",
    "    bad = 0\n",
    "    for _ in range(2000):\n",
    "        p, q = np.random.uniform(-box, box, 2), np.random.uniform(-box, box, 2)\n        if fn(X, y, (p + q) / 2) > (fn(X, y, p) + fn(X, y, q)) / 2 + 1e-10:\n            bad += 1\n    print(f\"   {name:<20}{bad:>5} violations of  J(mid) <= mean(J(a), J(b))\")\nprint(f\"   Hessian (2/n)X\u1e60X eigenvalues = {eig}   both > 0 -> a bowl\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. The Minus Sign\n",
    "\n",
    "Watch what happens if you accidentally flip a minus sign and do gradient *ascent* instead."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"4. THE MINUS SIGN   (identical init, identical alpha, opposite direction)\")\n",
    "print(f\"   {'iter':>5}{'descent  \u2212\u03b1\u2207J':>18}{'ascent  +\u03b1\u2207J':>18}\")\n",
    "td, tu = np.zeros(2), np.zeros(2)\n",
    "for i in range(41):\n",
    "    if i in (0, 5, 10, 20, 40):\n",
    "        print(f\"   {i:>5}{cost(X, y, td):>18.8f}{cost(X, y, tu):>18.6e}\")\n",
    "    if i < 40:\n",
    "        td, tu = td - alpha * grad(X, y, td), tu + alpha * grad(X, y, tu)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Automatic Braking\n",
    "\n",
    "Observe how the step shrinks purely because the gradient levels off, without any schedule."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"5. THE BRAKING IS FREE   (nothing in the loop shrinks the step)\")\n",
    "print(f\"   {'iter':>5}{'\u2016\u0394\u03b8\u2016':>12}{'\u2016\u2207J\u2016':>12}{'\u2016\u0394\u03b8\u2016/\u2016\u2207J\u2016':>12}{'shrink':>9}\")\n",
    "th, prev, early, late = np.zeros(2), None, 0.0, 0.0\n",
    "for i in range(1, 101):\n",
    "    g = grad(X, y, th)\n",
    "    gn = np.linalg.norm(g)\n",
    "    sn = alpha * gn\n",
    "    if i <= 10:\n",
    "        print(f\"   {i:>5}{sn:>12.6f}{gn:>12.6f}{sn / gn:>12.3f}\"\n",
              f\"{('\u2014' if prev is None else f'{sn / prev:.4f}'):>9}\")\n",
    "    early += sn if i <= 5 else 0.0\n",
    "    late += sn if i > 95 else 0.0\n",
    "    th, prev = th - alpha * g, sn\n",
    "print(f\"   predicted contraction  max|1 \u2212 \u03b1\u00b7\u03bb| = {np.abs(1 - alpha * eig).max():.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   distance travelled: first 5 iters {early:.6f}, last 5 of 100 {late:.3e},\"\n",
    "      f\" ratio {early / late:.3e}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Conditioning (Kappa)\n",
    "\n",
    "Observe how rescaling one feature stretches the circular bowl into a narrow canyon, and watch iterations climb linearly with the condition number."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"6. THE BOWL IS USUALLY A RAVINE   (feature 2 rescaled, own largest stable alpha)\")\n",
    "np.random.seed(43)\n",
    "x1, x2 = np.random.randn(n, 1), np.random.randn(n, 1)\n",
    "y2 = 3 * x1.ravel() + 1.5 * x2.ravel() + 7 + 0.5 * np.random.randn(n)\n",
    "print(f\"   {'scale':>7}{'kappa':>13}{'2/lambda_max':>15}{'iters':>9}   status\")\n",
    "for s in (1, 10, 100, 1000):\n",
    "    Xs = np.c_[np.ones(n), x1, x2 * s]\n",
    "    es = np.linalg.eigvalsh((2 / n) * (Xs.T @ Xs))\n",
    "    a_use = 0.9 * (2.0 / es.max())\n",
    "    floor = cost(Xs, y2, np.linalg.lstsq(Xs, y2, rcond=None)[0])\n",
    "    th, ok = np.zeros(3), False\n",
    "    for k in range(1, 200001):\n",
    "        th = th - a_use * grad(Xs, y2, th)\n",
    "        if cost(Xs, y2, th) - floor < 1e-6:\n",
    "            ok = True\n",
    "            break\n",
    "    print(f\"   x{s:>6}{es.max() / es.min():>13.1f}{2.0 / es.max():>15.6e}{k:>9}\"\n",
    "          f\"   {'converged' if ok else 'cap reached'}\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
